# Optional ML core runtime
# Cross-platform deterministic ML feature baseline.
# This file must remain installable on supported CI + local platforms.
# Run `make compile` in this directory to generate pinned ml-core.txt
#
# PLATFORM MATRIX (ADR-032):
#   OS:    Darwin (macOS), Linux
#   ISA:   arm64 (Apple Silicon), x86_64 (Intel/AMD)
#   Accel: cpu (default), mps (macOS ARM64), cuda (Linux x86_64)
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - Lockfiles must be compiled per-platform / per-index policy
# - CPU-only lockfiles should use the PyTorch CPU index in compilation
# - This layer EXCLUDES platform-specific packages (rawpy, coremltools)
# - This layer EXCLUDES SAM2 due to build-time torch requirements
# - Accel is EXPLICIT via profile, never inferred from OS
#
# SECURITY NOTE:
# - The supported Apple Silicon lane now anchors on torch==2.8.0 /
#   torchvision==0.23.0.
# - The frozen Darwin x86_64 and Linux lanes remain unsupported historical
#   baselines until retirement.
# - All torch.load() calls MUST use weights_only=True as defense in depth.
# - See: src/transformation_portal/core/security/torch_security.py for safe loading.
#
# See: requirements/README.md for layering rationale.

# --- PyTorch (deterministic, platform-aware) ---
# Supported lanes align with the repo-owned secure subprocess runtime.
#
# Platform-specific version notes:
# - macOS Intel (x86_64): frozen torch 2.2.2 historical baseline
# - macOS Apple Silicon (arm64): supported torch 2.8.0 baseline
# - Linux (all arch): frozen torch 2.8.0 historical baseline
#
# NOTE: When updating torch versions, verify SAM2/CLIP compatibility.

# macOS Intel (no modern torch builds after 2.2.x)
torch==2.2.2 ; platform_system == "Darwin" and platform_machine == "x86_64"  # CAS determinism
torchvision==0.17.2 ; platform_system == "Darwin" and platform_machine == "x86_64"  # CAS determinism

# macOS Apple Silicon (MPS)
torch==2.8.0 ; platform_system == "Darwin" and platform_machine == "arm64"  # Supported Apple Silicon baseline
torchvision==0.23.0 ; platform_system == "Darwin" and platform_machine == "arm64"  # Supported Apple Silicon pair

# Linux frozen historical baseline
torch==2.8.0 ; platform_system == "Linux"  # Frozen historical pin
torchvision==0.23.0 ; platform_system == "Linux"  # Frozen historical companion pin

